# hyprmod (pkg_extra.lst) writes its own live-settings config here, separate
# from hyprland.lua on purpose -- it's runtime state for a WIP GUI tool, not
# something this repo should ever track or accidentally commit.
Configs/configs/hypr/hyprland-gui.conf
Configs/configs/hypr/hyprland-gui.lua

# Per-user runtime state, rewritten by apply-theme.sh/apply_wallpaper.sh on
# every theme switch or wallpaper pick -- apply-theme.sh already falls back
# to $default_wallpaper when current-wallpaper.txt is missing, so these
# are safe to leave untracked rather than churning the repo with everyone's
# personal picks.
Configs/configs/theme-switcher/current-theme.json
Configs/configs/theme-switcher/themes/*/current-wallpaper.txt
Source/wallpapers/pywallpaper.jpg

# Key material. Nothing matching these is tracked today and nothing should
# be -- the rules exist so a stray `git add -A` in the repo root can't sweep
# up a private key that happens to be sitting there. That is not theoretical:
# an ssh keypair was found untracked in this repo's root, one careless add
# away from being published to a public remote.
#
# gitignore only covers UNTRACKED files, so this is a safety net, not a
# containment fix. A key belongs in ~/.ssh (0600), not in a dotfiles repo
# that gets pushed to GitHub. If one is ever actually committed, rotate it --
# removing the commit does not un-publish it.
key
key.pub
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*
id_dsa*
